/-!
# External L₁ module arguments for the linear-three case

The ordinary-A₆ representation exclusion is assembled from genuine structural
inputs: a noncentral chief section exists, its component restriction is paired,
its action is faithful, and neither component nor outer quadratic actors can
witness q ≤ 2. All section and model identifications are equivariant.

For the covered-A₆ branch, the actual generating seed supplies a natural tensor
chief section with the same point-parabolic marking. This excludes transvections
and, using 13.8.18(4), forces the marked V-actor to fill the point radical. Both
the proper and saturated critical-pair cases are excluded. The proper case's
index-two denominator and centralizer-lifting premises are proved from the
critical comparison and the tensor section.

These are separately usable conditional representation exclusions. Compatible
group-geometric identifications and exact earlier source clauses remain inputs
for the parent L₁-containment theorem; that full theorem is not asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.8.21(1), printed pp.956–957.
-/
